third_party/falcon_challenge
============================

This directory contains files adapted from the FALCON challenge repo:

  https://github.com/snel-repo/falcon-challenge

Licensed under MIT License (see `LICENSE`).

Files and modifications
-----------------------

- `filtering.py`
  Adapted from the FALCON filtering utils. Provides `apply_exponential_filter` and `NEURAL_TAU_MS`,
  the causal exponential smoother applied to spike-count features for both
  training and calibration.

- `spint_decoder.py`
  Adapted from the FALCON sample decoder. Rewritten to (a) load a SPINT
  Lightning checkpoint produced by `src/train.py`, (b) read all
  hyperparameters from the run's `.hydra/config.yaml`, (c) derive the
  calibration directory from the same Hydra config, (d) apply the
  exponential filter to calibration spikes when `smooth_calibration=True`,
  and (e) implement the `BCIDecoder` interface from `falcon_challenge`.

- `spint_sample.py`
  Adapted from the FALCON sample evaluation entry point. Modified to
  import `SpintDecoder` from this package.

- `spint_sample.Dockerfile`
  Adapted from the FALCON sample Dockerfile. Parameterized via
  `--build-arg TASK=<m1|m2|h1>` and `--build-arg BATCH_SIZE=...` so a
  single Dockerfile builds an image for any FALCON task. Bundles the
  packaged SPINT decoder pickle at `data/decoder.pkl`.
